<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Nov producer price index up 8.5 pct.</title>
<headline>S.African Nov producer price index up 8.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's all-commodities producer price index rose 0.5 percent in November from October after rising 1.3 percent in October, Central Statistical Service figures show.</p>
<p>The year-on-year rise in November was 8.5 percent after October's 8.3 percent rise.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast PPI would rise 0.7 percent month-on-month and 8.7 percent year-on-year.  </p>
<p>    Pct changes:	     Year/year		    month/month</p>
<p>			 Nov '96   Oct '96   Nov '95  - latest   prev</p>
<p>All commodities    8.5	 8.3	 8.3	  0.5	1.3</p>
<p>Locally produced   8.8	 8.5	 9.0	  0.5	0.8</p>
<p>Imported	     7.8	 7.7	 5.5	  0.1	3.0</p>
<p>Index (base 1995=100):</p>
<p>			 Nov '96   Oct '96   Nov '95</p>
<p>All commodities    110.3     109.8     101.7</p>
<p>Locally produced   111.1     110.5     102.1</p>
<p>Imported	     108.1     108.0     100.3</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
